          "comment": "Down in class; this opening handicap mark is a concern but 1m4f may well suit",
          "spotlight": "Won a novice at Sandown (1m2f, good) in April; ran creditably in defeat since in a Group 3 at York (1m2f, good to firm) and Listed race at Goodwood (1m2f, soft), particularly when third in the latter; this opening handicap mark is a concern but 1m4f may well suit.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-04-25",
              "horse": "Tattycoram",
              "horse_id": "hrs_44873724",
              "race": "bet365 'Wild Card' Fillies' Novice Stakes (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11589357",
              "course": "Sandown",
              "course_id": "crs_1404",
              "distance_f": "10",
              "distance_y": "2189",
              "quote": "Tattycoram was always a filly we liked, a proper model and as good a homebred as you'd come across. Very attractive. I'd say last year she was a bit fiery at the gates and we were just trying to stay on the right side of her. She had a good reintroduction at Yarmouth and I thought it was a good effort today. I'd say we'll play our cards on how she is in the coming weeks. I wouldn't rule out the Oaks entry she now has at all, but whatever we do will be with her best interests in mind rather than those of her trainer or owner. I'd love to see her at Epsom but that will depend on how she is over the next four or five weeks. We could have a look at Lingfield perhaps - Ralph Beckett, trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "She got a free pass for the Oaks after winning at Sandown on Friday and I wouldn't be against going. She got her own way up front, which always helps round there, but it was a good effort. We'll see how it develops. 28-04-25"
            }
          ],
