          "comment": "First 6f run for a while but he's down in class and should have a big run in him",
          "spotlight": "Stays further than this but fully effective at 6f; didn't get home having helped force the pace in the Buckingham Palace Stakes here (7f, good to firm) three weeks ago but it was still a solid effort; drops back into a Class 3 and he's an intriguing contender.",
          "quotes": [],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He did well from three to four and has been in good form this season, winning at Chester's May meeting and beaten no distance at Newmarket last time. He's got an entry in the Wokingham but the Buckingham Palace over seven furlongs looks tailor-made for him. He wouldn't want it too firm and if he could just get his toe in, that should be fine. 13-06-24"
            },
            {
              "quote": "He's a lightly raced colt who won over 7f first time out at Catterick this season. It was a rare runner for me there but it was the right race for him and he won like a nice horse. I didn't want to go to a big track and pick up a lofty handicap mark and that suited perfectly. I've given him an entry for the Jersey Stakes on Saturday, but he had a dirty scope last week and I‘ll have to speak to his owners before we decide whether to go. 21-06-23"
            }
          ],
