          "comment": "Ran better than 7th suggests on handicap debut; drop in trip should suit; far from exposed",
          "spotlight": "Won 6f novice at Goodwood last May in good style; 11 months off before hard-fought win at Wolverhampton in April; only seventh on his handicap debut at York Dante meeting (7f, good to firm) but he travelled well before meeting trouble at a crucial stage; returning to 6f could spark further progress.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-05-24",
              "horse": "Red Sand",
              "horse_id": "hrs_41189435",
              "race": "British Stallion Studs EBF Novice Stakes (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11267815",
              "course": "Goodwood",
              "course_id": "crs_546",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1320",
              "quote": "Red Sand was angelic in the prelims and I loved how straight and true he was. I didn't have company from a long way out but he never felt like being beaten. I loved the way he hit the line and he galloped out really well. He's a classy animal. He travelled well over five at Bath last time and I think the team expected him to be a little green that day. He's a proper professional and the response was immediate when I pressed the button. I don't see why he couldn't [be a Royal Ascot horse]. A stiff six furlongs would suit him there - Saffie Osborne, jockey."
            }
          ],
