          "comment": "Only midfield in the Queen Mary but pedigree suggests she should still do better",
          "spotlight": "Won well at Newmarket (good to firm) on 1,000 Guineas day for a promising debut; only midfield (behind Shine On Me) in the Queen Mary kept to 5f but pedigree suggests she should still do better, being out of a Listed scorer for her stable; by no means written off.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-05-04",
              "horse": "Spicy Marg",
              "horse_id": "hrs_52418142",
              "race": "Tattersalls £40,000 EBF Fillies' Novice Stakes (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11591268",
              "course": "Newmarket",
              "course_id": "crs_988",
              "distance_f": "5",
              "distance_y": "1100",
              "quote": "Spicy Marg did a nice piece of work ten days ago when she quickened up very nicely so we were hopeful coming here today. I trained her dam and when I saw this filly at the sales I was never going to be beaten in buying her. She'll go for the Marygate next - Michael Bell, trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "She's one of the top-rated two-year-old fillies in Britain. After she won at Newmarket in early May everything was working backwards from Royal Ascot and the Queen Mary. We ducked a couple of options at York and Carlisle with a view that we're saving our powder. We think she's very smart. With the ground, I wouldn't mind it fast but if it was very soft that would be an unknown. We really like her and she's my trainer's pick. 09-06-25"
            }
          ],
