          "comment": "Second run since wind surgery; needs to be at his peak and turf form is nowhere near that",
          "spotlight": "Reverted to Flat for new yard early this year and won three AW handicaps (1m6f/2m); given a wind operation (his second) in May and Northumberland Plate performance at Newcastle (2m, AW) 13 days ago was an interesting one, as he made smooth headway to dispute lead over 2f out but weakened in the final 1f; needs to be at his peak and turf form is nowhere near that.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-02-28",
              "horse": "Roaring Legend",
              "horse_id": "hrs_28013265",
              "race": "BetUK AWC Marathon Trial Handicap (GBBPlus Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11536031",
              "course": "Lingfield (AW)",
              "course_id": "crs_10218",
              "distance_f": "16",
              "distance_y": "3469",
              "quote": "Roaring Legend is really improving. He's taken a massive step forward since winning at Newcastle last time and Hugo is delighted with him. He got into a nice, even rhythm and I went forward going down the hill. He lengthened well and he's got a big engine. He gave me a nice feel and could progress into a Cup horse - David Probert, jockey."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He's been a wonderful addition to the yard. Everybody who rides him jokes that they'd pay to ride him every day. He's improved enormously, winning three times since joining us and switching back to the Flat. He may well get further than the two miles we've been campaigning him over. He'll go to Newcastle on Good Friday, when he'll have to give them all weight, and I'd have thought he'd be near enough favourite. The Melbourne Cup is the dream, so we'll need to qualify him for that and the Ormonde Stakes looks an obvious spot for him, although I've also put him in the Yorkshire Cup in case it comes up very soft at Chester. 09-04-25"
            },
            {
              "quote": "He made his debut in December when runner-up at Wolverhampton and followed with two similarly encouraging efforts over a mile. He has subsequently been gelded and I think he will be more effective on turf. He shows us speed at home but I think he is looking more like a 1m2f horse. I am happy with his opening mark of 78 and it would be wonderful to win a couple of races hopefully progressing onto better things. 29-03-23"
            }
          ],
