          "comment": "Has big-race form and back near his best when second to Insanity at Ayr on latest outing",
          "spotlight": "No win since 2023 but he was second in this race last year and third later on in both the Ebor at York (1m6f, good to firm) and November Handicap at Doncaster; back near his best when second to Insanity at Ayr on latest outing, so he's once again in each-way calculations.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-08-24",
              "horse": "Oneforthegutter",
              "horse_id": "hrs_25580702",
              "race": "Sky Bet Ebor Handicap (Heritage Handicap)",
              "race_id": "rac_11328512",
              "course": "York",
              "course_id": "crs_2782",
              "distance_f": "14",
              "distance_y": "3048",
              "quote": "I never expected Oneforthegutter to get in off his mark, but has run a huge race. He and Joe have just gelled together and ultimately just got outstayed. It was a huge performance and a little bit better than the what we were expecting. Class as much as anything beat him today but we'll look for similar sort of things. He could turn out in the Old Borough Cup at Haydock if it doesn't come around too quickly - Ian Williams, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-07-15",
              "horse": "Oneforthegutter",
              "horse_id": "hrs_25580702",
              "race": "Magnum Classic Ice Cream Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_10962276",
              "course": "Ascot",
              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "12",
              "distance_y": "2631",
              "quote": "Oneforthegutter has suffered with his wind in the past and that's his third run back after probably his third wind operation. You couldn't be confident the wind op had worked. As you can imagine [with his breathing] we were worried about the ground but Ben Curtis has given him a great ride and he's stuck at his task and stayed on well. He's always merited winning a prize like that and the new trip today was a good thing. It opens up options for him - Ian Williams, trainer."
            }
          ],
