          "owner": "Godolphin",
          "owner_id": "own_199380",
          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "Solid performer; ran creditably behind Crimson Advocate at Royal Ascot most recently",
          "spotlight": "Solid performer whose record of 11117112212 features wins in US Grade 1 contest last term and 1m1f Group 2 at Newmarket (good to firm; readily beat Elmalka) in May; ran creditably under a penalty behind Crimson Advocate at Royal Ascot (1m Group 2) most recently; strong contender.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-06-18",
              "horse": "Cinderella's Dream",
              "horse_id": "hrs_35596449",
              "race": "Duke Of Cambridge Stakes (Group 2) (Fillies & Mares)",
              "race_id": "rac_11649664",
              "course": "Ascot",
              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1753",
              "quote": "Cinderella's Dream ran a good, solid race. William [Buick] felt he had everything covered turning in, but didn't expect the winner to come over the top the way she did. William would prefer to see her back on a straight track, so we will head to the Falmouth Stakes next - Charlie Appleby, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2025-05-04",
              "horse": "Cinderella's Dream",
              "horse_id": "hrs_35596449",
              "race": "Betfred Dahlia Stakes (Group 2) (Fillies & Mares)",
              "race_id": "rac_11591242",
              "course": "Newmarket",
              "course_id": "crs_988",
              "distance_f": "9",
              "distance_y": "1980",
              "quote": "Cinderella's Dream has sharpened up over the last couple of weeks and Will [Buick] rode her with the confidence you just saw there. To be brutally honest, there was a bit of a tailwind there which can be an advantage when you are trying to drop one in. Our plan before today was to go back to Saratoga for the Diana Stakes and have a crack at that. I know Simon's [Crisford] filly [Choisya] is going back to America too so will be trying to keep away from her. The grand plan for this filly would be to work back from the Breeders' Cup Filly & Mare Turf once again - Charlie Appleby, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-08-02",
              "horse": "Cinderella's Dream",
              "horse_id": "hrs_35596449",
              "race": "Fasig-Tipton Saratoga Oaks Invitational Stakes (Grade 2) (3yo Fillies) (Mellon Course) (Turf)",
              "race_id": "rac_11356345",
              "course": "Saratoga",
              "course_id": "crs_11570",
              "distance_f": "9.5",
              "distance_y": "2090",
              "quote": "Cinderella's Dream is obviously a classy filly. The only reservation I had was that she put up such a big speed figure there last time that I was always concerned whether there would be a bounce after that. To be fair to the team, they were always confident that she was in good order. She's gone out there and done it comfortably. You could see that when William started taking her back on the turn and waiting instead of making that move earlier. He waited until the straight and just let her stride out under a hands-and-heels ride. We'll take a view on the Breeders' Cup. What she would take to that meeting would be plenty of experience and in the Breeders' Cup you need that along with a good draw - Charlie Appleby, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-03-02",
              "horse": "Cinderella's Dream",
              "horse_id": "hrs_35596449",
              "race": "Jumeirah 1000 Guineas Sponsored By Emirates SkyCargo (Listed Race) (Fillies) (Turf)",
              "race_id": "rac_11206338",
              "course": "Meydan",
              "course_id": "crs_32006",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1760",
              "quote": "Cinderella's Dream is four from four now and doing little wrong. The filly who won this last year went on to win the Guineas and while I'm not saying she's good enough to win one, she's certainly earning the right to run in one - Charlie Appleby, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-02-02",
              "horse": "Cinderella's Dream",
              "horse_id": "hrs_35596449",
              "race": "Jumeirah Fillies Classic Presented by Lincoln Aviator (Conditions Race) (Fillies) (Turf)",
              "race_id": "rac_11180728",
              "course": "Meydan",
              "course_id": "crs_32006",
              "distance_f": "7",
              "distance_y": "1540",
              "quote": "Cinderella's Dream was there for me the whole way. She's still learning on the job as she'd only had two previous starts. It was a good performance from a filly who I think is progressive. Mawj won this last year and went on to win the Guineas, so she's in good company and I wouldn't want to rule anything out - William Buick, jockey."
            }
          ],
