          "comment": "Better than ever when beating Cinderella's Dream to record a second Royal Ascot win",
          "spotlight": "5f performer when trained in USA; form figures of 0211 for current yard, most recently beating Cinderella's Dream in the Duke of Cambridge Stakes (1m Group 2; good to firm) to record a second Royal Ascot win and show career-best form; may rate higher still over this trip; respected.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-06-18",
              "horse": "Crimson Advocate",
              "horse_id": "hrs_35445662",
              "race": "Duke Of Cambridge Stakes (Group 2) (Fillies & Mares)",
              "race_id": "rac_11649664",
              "course": "Ascot",
              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "8",
              "distance_y": "1753",
              "quote": "Running Lion has got them all at it and suddenly the last half furlong she folded and I told James [McDonald] to settle Crimson Advocate where you're happy. This filly won a Queen Mary here two years ago and she's gone and got the mile better than the rest of them. Put it this way, we expected her to run well but not that well. Thady [Gosden] has spent a lot of time settling her from being a five furlong sprinter. When we ran her here last year and William Buick rode her in the King's Stand, he said 'John, she's looking for the bend' being an American filly but Thady has done a lovely job switching her job. When I said to James 'drop her out', he said 'are you sure?' and I said 'yes' - John Gosden, joint-trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2023-06-21",
              "horse": "Crimson Advocate",
              "horse_id": "hrs_35445662",
              "race": "Queen Mary Stakes (Group 2) (Fillies)",
              "race_id": "rac_10945233",
              "course": "Ascot",
              "course_id": "crs_52",
              "distance_f": "5",
              "distance_y": "1100",
              "quote": "We'll probably let the dust settle and come up with a plan. We'll see whether Crimson Advocate races in Europe again or we bring her home. We've a few days to think about it and are scheduled to fly back on June 28, so we'll make a plan between now and then - George Weaver, trainer."
            }
          ],
