          "comment": "Prolific last summer, winning five times; up and down this year and others appeal more",
          "spotlight": "Enjoyed a purple patch last summer, winning five times in 33 days; the latest success was off today's mark, albeit in a Class 6; retains ability but this won't be an easy race for her to dominate.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-05-31",
              "horse": "Jacquelina",
              "horse_id": "hrs_30822288",
              "race": "Trade Centre UK Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11269635",
              "course": "Chepstow",
              "course_id": "crs_312",
              "distance_f": "5",
              "distance_y": "1116",
              "quote": "I can't believe the amount Jacquelina has improved. It's kind of by default that she has because she ran on the heavy ground at Windsor and we didn't think she'd like it, but since she's run on soft ground she's just improved. To go and win like that today under a double penalty was pretty impressive. I wake up at about 8st 6lb and this saddle is about 2st! She's got an entry at Hamilton on Thursday but there's also a couple of options at Thirsk for her - Grace McEntee, jockey, speaking to Sky Sports Racing."
            }
          ],
