          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "Unpenalised for last year's C&D Group 2 win; could well progress again as a 3yo",
          "spotlight": "Three wins as a 2yo, notably the Group 2 Lowther Stakes over C&D last August (good to firm); soft ground perhaps no good to her when fifth of seven in the Cheveley Park Stakes when last seen; dam improved with age and quite possible she'll do even better this time around.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-08-22",
              "horse": "Celandine",
              "horse_id": "hrs_41564964",
              "race": "Sky Bet Lowther Stakes (Group 2) (Fillies) (IRE Incentive Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11328460",
              "course": "York",
              "course_id": "crs_2782",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1320",
              "quote": "Celandine is very tough. We were scratching our heads at Goodwood as she didn't look so tough that day. Today she was great and I'm buzzing. It's all about the Cheveley Park for her now and hopefully the Breeders' Cup - Ed Walker, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2024-06-29",
              "horse": "Celandine",
              "horse_id": "hrs_41564964",
              "race": "Maureen Brittain Memorial Empress Fillies' Stakes (Listed Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11302187",
              "course": "Newmarket (July)",
              "course_id": "crs_4524",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1320",
              "quote": "Celandine has got loads of boot and is very tough and Tom thinks she is not done yet. I don't think we'll be going up in trip even though she's in the Moyglare Stud Stakes, and we may have to supplement her for something nice - Ed Walker, trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "She's been a star and the Cheveley Park is the obvious next step having won the Lowther. She's had ten days out in the paddock to freshen her up, which is what we did after Goodwood and before York, and she looks fantastic. She's back cantering and hopefully will be spot on for Newmarket. 11-09-24"
            },
            {
              "quote": "She was a star last year, winning the Lowther Stakes, and we have big hopes for her this season. We never toyed with any idea of the 1,000 Guineas and we're going to stick at 6f. We'll start her in the Kilvington Stakes over 6f at Newmarket - she has no penalty so it makes sense. After that she could maybe go to Haydock and then the Commonwealth Cup, unless she tells us otherwise. 16-04-25"
            }
          ],
