          "owner": "Jaber Abdullah",
          "owner_id": "own_11164",
          "prev_trainers": [],
          "prev_owners": [],
          "comment": "Improving 3yo; good fourth in Royal Ascot Group 1 latest; leading claims at this level",
          "spotlight": "Lightly raced 3yo who is improving all the time, winning a conditions race on AW in April before a good third in Listed company at Newbury one month later; fine fourth in the Group 1 Commonwealth Cup at Royal Ascot three weeks ago, keeping on well; open to further progress and this test should suit; key player.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-04-18",
              "horse": "Sayidah Dariyan",
              "horse_id": "hrs_44721761",
              "race": "bet365 Conditions Stakes (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11578645",
              "course": "Chelmsford (AW)",
              "course_id": "crs_28158",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1320",
              "quote": "I wouldn't normally take on horses rated 110 when you're 92 but Sayidah Dariyan was working really well at home. She could come back here in two weeks [Chelmer Fillies' Stakes], but I wouldn't be mad about that, or go for the Carnarvon which would be spot on - Richard Hughes, trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "I was thrilled with her run in the Carnarvon at Newbury. The winner Symbol Of Honour can't run in the Commonwealth Cup as he's a gelding, so you can discount him, and it was only her second run on grass. She can only improve and she'll go there with a little squeak. 10-06-25"
            },
            {
              "quote": "We really fancied her at Windsor at the start of the month, but she stumbled over every one of those ridges and it was hard to get her on an even keel. I backed her up just over a week later because it was the ideal race over 6f at Lingfield on the all-weather. I didn't think she'd win like she did and she's gone up in her estimation at home. We might go to Dundalk on October 4 for a Listed race over 5f. 18-09-24"
            }
          ],
