          "comment": "Two wins this year, the latest at Doncaster last week; not well in under a penalty",
          "spotlight": "Come-from-behind sprinter with two 5f wins this year, more recently in a small field at Doncaster last week; not well in under a 4lb penalty though and he was well held in this race last year.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2025-07-04",
              "horse": "Muker",
              "horse_id": "hrs_21649495",
              "race": "Talasey Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_11664302",
              "course": "Doncaster",
              "course_id": "crs_390",
              "distance_f": "5",
              "distance_y": "1103",
              "quote": "Muker really tries for you and everything was perfect. I can't take too much credit as he's a great horse and Nigel has done a great job with him. He's so genuine, tries so hard and when I saw the pace they were going, I thought \"happy days\" - Faye McManoman, jockey, speaking to Sky Sports Racing."
            },
            {
              "date": "2020-07-09",
              "horse": "Muker",
              "horse_id": "hrs_21649495",
              "race": "Download The ITV App British Stallion Studs EBF Novice Stakes (Plus 10 Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_9890881",
              "course": "York",
              "course_id": "crs_2782",
              "distance_f": "5",
              "distance_y": "1100",
              "quote": "Muker's form has worked out well and he'll go for the Molecomb in three weeks. He's all speed - but for a horse with so much speed he has a great mind. - Paul Mulrennan, rider"
            },
            {
              "date": "2020-06-02",
              "horse": "Muker",
              "horse_id": "hrs_21649495",
              "race": "Betway / British Stallion Studs EBF Maiden Stakes (Div I)",
              "race_id": "rac_9848956",
              "course": "Newcastle (AW)",
              "course_id": "crs_35178",
              "distance_f": "5",
              "distance_y": "1100",
              "quote": "Muker was supposed to go to Doncaster, he was ready to go the first day and Phil's done a good job to keep him ticking along nicely until now. He's been really good at home, we've done plenty with him and we make sure they know their job, which he did today. He's been really professional and he couldn't have done it nicer. The owner will be absolutely thrilled to go to Ascot, if he won or ran well today that was the plan. - Sammy Jo Bell, partner of winning trainer Philip Makin"
            }
          ],
