          "comment": "Flat winner, has shown ability over hurdles, unlucky to unseat on latest, place chance",
          "spotlight": "Locally trained mare is 3-17 on the Flat; 0-4 over hurdles but ran well when a 3.75l second of 9 in a mares' maiden hurdle at Thurles (2m, good) last November; still in contention when hampered and unseating two out at Tipperary latest; place chance.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2022-09-24",
              "horse": "Mile End",
              "horse_id": "hrs_30822183",
              "race": "Barberstown Castle Nursery Handicap",
              "race_id": "rac_10687885",
              "course": "Curragh",
              "course_id": "crs_4628",
              "distance_f": "6",
              "distance_y": "1320",
              "quote": "I fancied Mile End in Down Royal the last day but she was drawn 11, missed the kick and never got into the race. Ben [Coen] said he was forced wide all the way, stayed on well and probably wants a mile, but I worked her in blinkers the other day, gave her a sharpener, and they seemed to have brought her alive. It looked like a winnable nursery. She got out there in front, flowing along, and Ben said she did it well - Johnny Murtagh, trainer."
            }
          ],
