          "comment": "Better for recent comeback run but regressive profile",
          "spotlight": "Hasn't looked a natural over fences but won a Grade 2 handicap chase at Cheltenham in April last year (2m4f, good) for Harry Fry; badly out of form since, although entitled to come on for recent comeback run (yard debut) at Punchestown.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2024-04-17",
              "horse": "In Excelsis Deo",
              "horse_id": "hrs_32264330",
              "race": "Matt Hampson Foundation Silver Trophy Handicap Chase (Grade 2) (A Limited Handicap) (GBB Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11222458",
              "course": "Cheltenham",
              "course_id": "crs_286",
              "distance_f": "20.5",
              "distance_y": "4527",
              "quote": "I'm relieved to finally get his head in front. In Excelsis  Deo has been running well and stayed consistent without having the luck in running. Johnny [Burke] has given him a lovely ride, nursing him into it and we thought at the bottom of the hill this was the closest he'd been all season so we just hoped he'd come up the hill as he had done on a few runs previously. We'll see what happens from here but enjoy this first. We've been in various spots in this winner's enclosure so it's good to have finally won - Harry Fry, trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "He took us by surprise with how he won on his chasing debut at Hereford and then got found out against more experienced horses after a hike in the handicap. His last run was over two miles and I think that's where he'll start his campaign. I hope there's more to come. 04-10-23"
            }
          ],
