          "comment": "Clear 2nd to Mica Malpic at Roscommon shows him in good order; 5lb rise though; reserve",
          "spotlight": "Third reserve; four-time hurdles winner is 0-7 chasing but recent clear second to Mica Malpic at Roscommon shows him in good order; 5lb rise to contend with now though.",
          "quotes": [
            {
              "date": "2023-08-05",
              "horse": "Ambitious Fellow",
              "horse_id": "hrs_23056061",
              "race": "BoyleSports Handicap Hurdle (Listed Race)",
              "race_id": "rac_11002446",
              "course": "Galway",
              "course_id": "crs_4758",
              "distance_f": "22.5",
              "distance_y": "4980",
              "quote": "Ambitious Fellow lost his form and there was an issue with him after he ran at Limerick last year, but he looks back to himself now. I was worried about the ground but it worked out great - Peter Fahey, trainer."
            },
            {
              "date": "2022-09-24",
              "horse": "Ambitious Fellow",
              "horse_id": "hrs_23056061",
              "race": "Allman Contracts Novice Hurdle",
              "race_id": "rac_10687677",
              "course": "Listowel",
              "course_id": "crs_4940",
              "distance_f": "20",
              "distance_y": "4400",
              "quote": "Ambitious Fellow has great form and he was unlucky [when brought down] at the Galway festival, with the rain also coming. He's a novice for this season in the UK because of the timing of his Punchestown win. He has plenty of experience and the trip of two miles and five furlongs at Cheltenham in November would suit him. Once the ground goes soft he'll get a break - Peter Fahey, trainer"
            },
            {
              "date": "2022-04-27",
              "horse": "Ambitious Fellow",
              "horse_id": "hrs_23056061",
              "race": "Connolly's RED MILLS Irish EBF Auction Hurdle Series Final",
              "race_id": "rac_10539542",
              "course": "Punchestown",
              "course_id": "crs_5070",
              "distance_f": "20",
              "distance_y": "4360",
              "quote": "Ambitious Fellow was bought to be sold but we brought him across to Doncaster and couldn't get anyone to buy him - Peter Fahey, trainer."
            }
          ],
          "stable_tour": [
            {
              "quote": "The ground was just far too soft for him at Wetherby and, with the benefit of hindsight, I probably shouldn't have run him. I've an eye on the big three mile handicap hurdle at Navan worth €100,000 next month if the ground isn't too soft. We're really looking forward to sending him over fences next season. 27-11-23"
            },
            {
              "quote": "I thought he was impressive in winning his bumper at Fairyhouse. He was bought to be sold and we brought him to the sales after Fairyhouse but we weren't getting enough for him so we brought him home. In hindsight he should never have run over hurdles at Clonmel last month as it was a bit soon after being over at the sales. He didn't jump great that day but he jumps well at home and the plan is to get a run or two into him before the auction series final at Punchestown in the spring. 08-12-21"
            }
          ],
